Every clinician should prescribe an as-needed-opioid for a moderate-to-severe-pain and should advise an as-needed-opioid for a moderate-to-severe-pain and should avoid a scheduled-opioid.
An as-needed-opioid-example contains 5 hydrocodone-milligrams and contains 325 acetaminophen-milligrams and uses 1 tablet per 4 hours for a moderate-to-severe-pain.
If a patient has a prolonged-around-the-clock-opioid-use for a few-day-period then every clinician should encourage an opioid-taper and should recommend an opioid-taper.
